From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] Digits: numpad in landscape, digit row in portrait

The landscape layout, the only one shown, had no digits: a numeric
password could not be typed.  Landscape gets a numpad on the right
(7 8 9, 4 5 6, 1 2 3, 0), keeping four rows; a new portrait layout puts
a digit row above the same keys, as the screen is narrow.  The portrait
layout is used when GTKLOCK_VIRTKB_PORTRAIT is set (pro1x-lock sets it
in portrait).
---
--- a/layout.mobintl.h
+++ b/layout.mobintl.h
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 	Nav,
 	Landscape,
 	LandscapeSpecial,
+	Portrait,
 	ComposeA,
 	ComposeE,
 	ComposeY,
@@ -70,7 +71,7 @@
 
